I am a mathematician, no previous knowledge in design. No project
management experience either. This is completely non-commercial, so in
true Do-It-Yourself style we learn as we go along. We are not
designing a rocket-launching device, but a roguelike. Feedback,
relying on established design principles and thinking carried us this
far.

To be honest, I think that Nethack lacks game design. There are very
many good odds and ends (many of them highly polished), but then
rendered useless by some huge balance hole. I cannot see overarching
designs. except possibly for: a) every game is winnable and b)
explictly not ruling out scumming. (Scumming as in: repeated, tedious
actions which provide benefits over time, at little or no risk. It is
then up to the players to decide whether they scum or not. This adds a
strategic choice, I am aware of that.)

